WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.659
Grandpa, is what the Bible says true?

2
00:00:03.953 --> 00:00:05.829
Yes. Look at the bird!

3
00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:09.241
And the tree that grew from a tiny seed.

4
00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:12.225
To me, it is clear that God exists.

5
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:17.683
And the Bible describes reality
and people in a way I recognise.

6
00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:25.593
As I read and pray, my faith grows and life
makes sense in the light of the Bible.

7
00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:29.106
But how can we know what
happened so long ago?

8
00:00:29.912 --> 00:00:34.481
We investigate old texts and
other clues, as historians do.

9
00:00:35.703 --> 00:00:39.979
The Bible is many books written
and collected over a long time.

10
00:00:39.979 --> 00:00:44.322
Historical research supports
important parts of several of them.

11
00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.386
Look here in Luke, for example.

12
00:00:47.386 --> 00:00:52.224
He investigated carefully and drew
on accounts from eyewitnesses.

13
00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:54.527
Like a detective?

14
00:00:55.075 --> 00:00:57.483
Now it is your turn to investigate.

15
00:00:57.483 --> 00:00:59.066
We travel back to Luke.

16
00:00:59.066 --> 00:01:03.883
He is gathering accounts about Jesus
— and you will be his apprentice.

17
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.266
Listen to the witnesses.

18
00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.250
Look for clues.

19
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.986
What can they tell us about what happened?

20
00:01:12.175 --> 00:01:13.997
The game story is fictional,

21
00:01:13.997 --> 00:01:18.031
but along the way you encounter
texts and clues from the past.

22
00:01:18.031 --> 00:01:20.698
You get to try thinking like a historian.

23
00:01:21.495 --> 00:01:22.340
There you are!

24
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.541
Come, we have something to
investigate in the square.

